{%- comment -%}
  Naira Flore — The Journal (blog index)
  Ported from src/pages/Journal.tsx (Lovable repo).

  The Lovable page mapped over a hardcoded array (src/data/seoContent.ts →
  allArticles). Per the port contract that data is NOT copied in: this renders
  `blog.articles`, so the merchant owns the posts in Shopify.

  Kept from the source: engraved 01/02/03 index, gold hairline that draws in,
  date · read-time meta line, "READ THE GUIDE" underline, drifting arrow.

  Three things worth knowing before editing:

  1. No pagination. Journal.tsx maps the whole array and shows all 19 posts on
     one page, so no paginate tag is used here — without one Shopify returns up
     to 50 articles, which covers the blog with room to spare. Add one back only
     if the blog ever passes 50 posts, and expect the page to stop matching
     React the moment it does.

  2. Ordering. Journal.tsx renders source-array order; Shopify hands back
     `blog.articles` newest-published first, and the store's published dates do
     not run in the source order. Sorting by id restores it — the 19 posts were
     created in that order, so id rises with it — and it also keeps the engraved
     01..19 index stable, which a date sort would not.

  3. Read time. The Lovable `readTime` is hand-written per article (its posts
     run 44–73 words/minute, so no wpm formula reproduces it) and Shopify has no
     equivalent field. It is read from an OPTIONAL `custom.read_time` integer
     metafield on the article, falling back to a 200 wpm estimate off the body
     when the metafield is absent — same graceful-degrade pattern as
     product.metafields.custom.materials in nf-product.liquid. The live store
     has no such metafields yet; until they are seeded the line reads an
     estimate rather than the authored number.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'nf-tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'nf-content.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign posts = blog.articles | sort: 'id' -%}

<div class="nf-journal">
  <div class="nf-journal__wrap">
    <header class="nf-journal__masthead">
      <div class="nf-journal__wash" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="nf-kicker">{{ section.settings.kicker | escape }}</p>
      <h1>{{ section.settings.heading | default: blog.title | escape }}</h1>
      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <p class="nf-journal__intro">{{ section.settings.intro | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="nf-journal__hairline" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </header>

    {%- if posts.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="nf-journal__list">
        {%- for article in posts -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign minutes = article.metafields.custom.read_time.value
            if minutes == blank
              assign words = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
              assign minutes = words | divided_by: 200 | at_least: 1
            endif
            assign summary = article.excerpt_or_content | strip_html | strip | truncatewords: 45
          -%}
          <li>
            <article class="nf-journal__entry">
              <a href="{{ article.url }}">
                <span class="nf-journal__index" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
                <span>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    React renders the date, a padded middot and the read time as
                    three adjacent children with no whitespace between them, so
                    the meta line's own text is "10 February 20265 min read".
                    Keep this on one line — a newline here becomes a space and
                    the element stops matching.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="nf-journal__meta">{{ article.published_at | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>{{ minutes }} min read</span>
                  <span class="nf-journal__title">{{ article.title | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if summary != blank -%}
                    <span class="nf-journal__excerpt">{{ summary }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="nf-journal__more">{{ section.settings.read_label | escape }}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="nf-journal__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </article>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="nf-journal__empty">{{ section.settings.empty_text | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Naira journal",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "nf-journal-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "NAIRA FLORE · THE JOURNAL" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Guides from the atelier" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "How to size a ring at home, how to keep a gold finish from failing, what zirconia actually is, and how to put an Indo-Western look together. Written by the people who make the pieces."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "read_label", "label": "Read link label", "default": "READ THE GUIDE" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "empty_text",
      "label": "Empty state",
      "default": "The first guides from the atelier are being written. Check back shortly."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Naira journal" }]
}
{% endschema %}
